[1;38;2;133;131;146mRun the program[m                                                                                     
  [1;38;2;241;239;239ms space[m    run to the next step anywhere, including inside this one                               
  [1;38;2;241;239;239mn[m          run this step whole; stop at the next step at this level or above                      
  [1;38;2;241;239;239mf[m          run until the loop, parallel, switch, or call around this step is left                 
  [1;38;2;241;239;239mc[m          run to the next breakpoint, or the end                                                 
  [1;38;2;241;239;239mb[m          return to the previous stop (a session that can step back)                             
  [1;38;2;241;239;239mr[m          return to the nearest earlier breakpoint stop, or the first                            
  [1;38;2;241;239;239mg[m          go to a point of the timeline, counted from 0, in one move (a session that can travel) 
  [1;38;2;241;239;239mp[m          hold at the next step boundary                                                         
                                                                                                    
[1;38;2;133;131;146mMove[m                                                                                                
  [1;38;2;241;239;239mup k[m       move up a row                                                                          
  [1;38;2;241;239;239mdown j[m     move down a row                                                                        
  [1;38;2;241;239;239menter[m      open or close the row (click too); in the flow, run until it                           
  [1;38;2;241;239;239mright l[m    open the row; in the flow, unfold it                                                   
  [1;38;2;241;239;239mleft h[m     close the row, or go to its parent; in the flow, fold it                               
  [1;38;2;241;239;239mPgUp[m       up a page                                                                              
  [1;38;2;241;239;239mPgDn[m       down a page                                                                            
  [1;38;2;241;239;239mhome[m       first row                                                                              
  [1;38;2;241;239;239mend G[m      last row                                                                               
                                                                                                    
[1;38;2;133;131;146mScreen[m                                                                                              
  [1;38;2;241;239;239mtab[m        focus the next pane (click a pane to focus it)                                         
  [1;38;2;241;239;239mshift+tab[m  focus the previous pane                                                                
  [1;38;2;241;239;239m: /[m        type a command; every verb below works there                                           
  [1;38;2;241;239;239mi[m          inspect the selected scope row in the console                                          
                                                                                                    
